// The question-to-flag plan as data (Story S5). docs/QUESTION-FLAG-PLAN.md is the human contract for the
// flag stories S6 to S11; this module is the same plan in a form the tests can check. The tests
// (tests/data/questions.test.mjs) enforce that every asked question is read by at least one planned flag,
// that every question a flag reads exists and can be visible together with the others, that ids, buckets,
// kinds, domains and priorities are valid, that the facts and sources named exist in research/ and the
// registry, and that the tables in the plan document match this data.
//
// Fields per flag
//   id          kebab-case flag id the owning story creates
//   story       S6 .. S11 (the owner; only that story edits the flag file)
//   file        the flags/<file>.mjs it lives in (see `files` for each story's ownership)
//   bucket      raise | drop | question
//   kind        cross-policy | within-policy | education
//   domain      the flag domain (engine DOMAINS)
//   priority    inside the story's range (see `ranges`); lower sorts first within a bucket
//   status      planned | conditional (conditional = cannot ship until its condition is met)
//   questions   asked question ids the flag reads (ctx.answer / is / includes / option / isNotSure / cards)
//   holds       policy ids it reads (ctx.holds); `policies` (Q1, the question those ids are ticked in) is listed
//               first in `questions` whenever `holds` is not empty
//   trigger     when it fires, in one sentence, including Not sure handling
//   factIds     research fact ids the copy may rest on (research/*.mjs)
//   sourceIds   registry source ids to cite (each must be a source of at least one listed fact)
//   wording     what the research could not support, i.e. how the copy must be worded

